  "body": "https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/images.html#reacting-to-environment-changes before step 14.4 ... it seems this part of the spec doesn't pay any attention to the `loading` attribute currently. The spec doesn't say when to run this algorithm, so there's leeway there, but it's not ideal imo. A change to the environment shouldn't cause a lazy outside-viewport `img` to load, right?\r\n\r\n_Originally posted by @zcorpan in https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/7237#issuecomment-949929691_",
